    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "A supermarket charges $\\frac{b}{3}$ dollars for $b$ kg of potatoes, and $\\frac{c}{2}$ dollars for $c$ kg of oranges. If 12 kg of potatoes and 10 kg of oranges are bought, what is the cost?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$9$",
      "worked": "Substitute $b=12$ and $c=10$ into the total cost, in dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{b}{3}+\\frac{c}{2}&=\\frac{12}{3}+\\frac{10}{2}\\\\\\frac{b}{3}+\\frac{c}{2}&=4+5\\\\\\frac{b}{3}+\\frac{c}{2}&=9\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe total cost is $\\$9$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
